{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: PI and PID loops",
  "exampleId": "block-control-loops",
  "description": "Each plant is a lag with τ = 0.5 s and each loop follows a unit step at 0.1 s. Every controller takes the reference and the measurement and forms the error itself. The continuous PI and PID are the Modelica library controllers: gain 1, integral time 0.5 s (so the integral gain is 2), and for the PID a derivative time of 0.05 s filtered at a tenth of it; the sampled ones run at 1 kHz with the same gains and reproduce exactly in exported C. All four reach the set point with no steady error, because each has integral action. Change a gain and run again to compare.",
  "duration": 4,
  "revision": 0,
  "blocks": [
